# Every tracked file listed in MANIFEST.sha256 is sealed by the SHA-256 of its exact
# bytes (`sha256sum -c MANIFEST.sha256`). With core.autocrlf=true, the Git for Windows
# default, checkout rewrites LF to CRLF, so the same commit gave a different verdict
# on Windows than on Linux. `-text` turns off line-ending conversion for the sealed
# set, so checkout writes the committed blob on every platform and the check gives
# one verdict everywhere. MANIFEST.sha256 is pinned too: a CRLF copy puts a carriage
# return on each path and sha256sum then cannot open any listed file.
# Root-level paths start with "/" so they do not also match files in subfolders.
# Files outside the manifest (LICENSE-TEXT, docs/, .github/) keep default handling.
/.gitignore -text
/00-ABSTRACT.md -text
/DEMO-two-minds.md -text
/ENDGAME.md -text
/LICENSE -text
/MANIFEST.sha256 -text
/PRINCIPLE.md -text
/README.md -text
/THESIS.md -text
/VERDICT.md -text
/center.py -text
/vision-arm-REPORT.md -text
center/** -text
sims/** -text
